  summary:
    "The Letter to the Hebrews and its high-priestly Christ; James, 1 and 2 Peter, Jude, and the letters of John; the Book of Revelation, its world and its long history of interpretation; Christians under Roman persecution; and how twenty-seven books came to be recognized as the New Testament.",
